```

Verify:

- the exact construction method for each strategy;
- when candles become visible;
- whether only completed candles are used;
- whether fill logic can see future candle information;
- when risk and quantity are calculated;
- how spread, commission and slippage are applied;
- whether management decisions use information unavailable at that moment;
- whether all feature switches really alter runtime behaviour;
- whether generated artifacts accurately describe the configuration used.

## Flow B — policy promotion

```text
Completed simulation/research configuration
→ policy-profile generation
→ artifact validation
→ configuration hash
→ review/promotion status
→ live host loading
```

Verify:

- the promoted policy uses the simulator’s actual resolved configuration;
- no values are reconstructed through a second divergent mapper;
- configuration hashes are stable and deterministic;
- artifact IDs and content hashes are validated;
- strategy and feature-schema compatibility are checked;
- approved live policy cannot silently mutate;
- a live deployment cannot independently retune Agent, risk, portfolio or management logic;
- deployment-only values remain outside the strategy policy.

## Flow C — observe/shadow live operation

```text
Broker pricing
+ authoritative completed candles
→ normalized market events
→ per-market actor
→ multi-timeframe snapshots
→ ChartAnnotator
→ Agent
→ calibration/meta-label
→ trading conditions
→ neutral candidate
→ shadow/observe handling
→ diagnostics/outcome tracking
```

Verify:

- strategic decisions use completed candles only;
- quote data is used only where appropriate;
- reconnect catch-up does not produce duplicate historical decisions;
- no trigger interval is evaluated twice;
- market actors remain isolated;
- a failure in one market does not corrupt another;
- cross-market data uses only information available at the decision time;
- epoch coordination cannot omit or duplicate candidates;
- shadow Agents cannot reserve capital or send orders.

